# Reading: the spread (hot end / interfaces / cold end) is proportional to the outer tolerance and independent of
# the linear tolerance -> it is heat leaking through the ADIABATIC arcs, whose zero-gradient value is lagged one
# Picard iteration (flux = Df * (T_P - T_P,previous), |dT| <= tolerance). Interface 1 == interface 2 to 13 digits;
# at tolerance 1e-12 every line agrees to 7.5e-10 Q. Predicted leak per block ~ (20..45 faces per arc) x Df(1.26 inner,
# 2.5 outer) x dT(<=1e-8) matches the gate-run spreads 5.2e-7 / 7.6e-7 / 1.15e-6 (grows 1.5x per refinement = face count).
# The T L2 error at converged tolerance is 3.9e-7 on 12x30: the scheme reproduces T linear in theta almost exactly,
# so the gate-run T errors (1.5e-6 / 7.3e-7 / 6.9e-7) are dominated by iteration error -> order 0.147 on the fine pair.

